<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Apply Reverse</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from the</span> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>tree context menu</b></span> <span class="Path">for</span> <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Transformation &gt; Apply Reverse</b></span></i><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p class="Description"><b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span></b> <span class="Command">Apply Reverse</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command transforms visible selected entities by applying the reversed transformation matrix. Transformations may include translation, rotation, and scale depending on the alignments transformation matrix. The inverted matrix is applied to all points of the selected entities.</span></p>
<p><span class="Command">Apply Reverse</span> <span lang="EN-GB">is grayed if there are no selected entities.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Entities of any type can be transformed. This command works on entire entity, no matter if it is selected wholly or partially. If you have partial selection KUBE will issue a warning message about this.</span></p>
